# The committed evidence in `data/` is compared **byte for byte** against what the
# pipeline writes — `crawl/sitemap-extract.test.mjs` asserts "the file was not
# edited by hand" by rebuilding it and comparing the string.
#
# The writers emit LF. A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites the
# working copy to CRLF, so the bytes on disk stop being the bytes the reduction
# gives, and that test fails on Windows while it passes on CI. The file in git was
# always LF; it was the checkout that changed it.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working copy, so the evidence is the same bytes everywhere.
data/*.json text eol=lf
